{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QNMBjHwHkFbPCW36pNXnR7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: prd020-true\n     2→title: \"cmd/true: Exit Successfully\"\n     3→\n     4→problem: |\n     5→  Shell scripts use true as a no-op command that always succeeds. It appears in conditional\n     6→  expressions, while loops (while true; do ...; done), and as a placeholder in pipelines.\n     7→  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtrue, installed by\n     8→  coreutils) in exit code behavior and output, verified by differential testing via\n     9→  pkg/testutils under LC_ALL=C.\n    10→\n    11→goals:\n    12→  - G1: Exit with status 0 unconditionally, matching GNU true exit behavior.\n    13→  - G2: Handle --help and --version flags, matching GNU true flag handling.\n    14→\n    15→requirements:\n    16→  R1:\n    17→    title: Exit status\n    18→    items:\n    19→      - R1.1: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with no arguments.\n    20→      - R1.2: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with any arguments that are not --help or --version. Arguments are not parsed, validated, or acted upon; they are silently ignored.\n    21→      - R1.3: Must not read from stdin under any circumstances.\n    22→      - R1.4: Must not write to stdout or stderr under normal operation (no arguments or unrecognized arguments).\n    23→\n    24→  R2:\n    25→    title: Flag handling (--help, --version)\n    26→    items:\n    27→      - R2.1: When --help is the first argument, must print a usage message to stdout and exit 0. Remaining arguments after --help are ignored.\n    28→      - R2.2: When --version is the first argument, must print version information to stdout and exit 0. Remaining arguments after --version are ignored.\n    29→      - R2.3: Only the first argument is checked for --help and --version. If --help or --version appears in any position other than the first argument, it is ignored and true exits 0 silently.\n    30→\n    31→  R3:\n    32→    title: Operand behavior\n    33→    items:\n    34→      - R3.1: All operands (non-flag arguments) are silently ignored. true does not distinguish between flags and operands; everything except --help and --version as the first argument is discarded.\n    35→      - R3.2: The \"--\" end-of-options marker has no special meaning to true. It is ignored like any other argument.\n    36→\n    37→  R4:\n    38→    title: SIGPIPE handling\n    39→    items:\n    40→      - R4.1: |\n    41→          Must install a SIGPIPE handler at startup using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler, matching\n    42→          the pattern used by other utilities in the project (see cmd/cat/main.go). This ensures\n    43→          silent exit when stdout is closed by a downstream consumer in a pipeline.\n    44→\n    45→  R5:\n    46→    title: Error handling and exit codes\n    47→    items:\n    48→      - R5.1: Must exit 0 in all cases except a write error during --help or --version output.\n    49→      - R5.2: If a write error occurs while printing --help or --version output (e.g., SIGPIPE or full disk), must exit 1.\n    50→      - R5.3: \"Error messages for write failures must be written to stderr in the format: \\\"true: <error description>\\\".\"\n    51→      - R5.4: Must not exit with any status other than 0 or 1.\n    52→\n    53→non_goals:\n    54→  - cmd/true does not implement any flags beyond --help and --version.\n    55→  - cmd/true does not perform any computation or I/O beyond the optional help/version output.\n    56→  - cmd/true does not read from stdin or process piped input.\n    57→\n    58→acceptance_criteria:\n    59→  - \"AC1: go run ./cmd/true; echo $? prints 0.\"\n    60→  - \"AC2: go run ./cmd/true foo bar --baz; echo $? prints 0.\"\n    61→  - \"AC3: go run ./cmd/true --help prints a usage message to stdout and exits 0.\"\n    62→  - \"AC4: go run ./cmd/true --version prints version information to stdout and exits 0.\"\n    63→  - \"AC5: Differential test against gtrue passes with LC_ALL=C for no-args, arbitrary-args, and single-unrecognized-flag cases, comparing exit codes.\"\n    64→  - \"AC6: Differential test verifies no stdout or stderr output when invoked without --help or --version, under LC_ALL=C.\"\n    65→  - \"AC7: cmd/true compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    66→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EbL9EiwfcGCQq9hrFV7MRQ","session_id":"8b8e2752-e0d3-4adb-aeb5-99f03f790516","uuid":"fb127d58-4de5-49bc-bd5f-445197dfc6e2"}
