{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S8S2ypFnSQcU3dGNwsu5Sx","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: go-unix-utils-roadmap\n     2→title: \"go-unix-utils Release Road Map\"\n     3→\n     4→releases:\n     5→  - version: \"00.0\"\n     6→    name: \"Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure\"\n     7→    status: spec_complete\n     8→    description: |\n     9→      Specify and verify the build lifecycle and shared library infrastructure that all\n    10→      subsequent releases depend on. This release covers magefiles/ (build, lint, clean,\n    11→      install targets and cmd/version), pkg/testutils (differential testing harness),\n    12→      pkg/sys (syscall abstractions), and pkg/format (output formatting). The cmd/version\n    13→      binary is the first compiled artifact and the smoke test for the build pipeline.\n    14→    use_cases:\n    15→      - id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n    16→        status: spec_complete\n    17→      - id: rel00.0-uc002-format\n    18→        status: spec_complete\n    19→      - id: rel00.0-uc003-sys\n    20→        status: spec_complete\n    21→      - id: rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n    22→        status: spec_complete\n    23→\n    24→  - version: \"01.0\"\n    25→    name: \"Batch 1 — wc specification and differential test\"\n    26→    status: spec_complete\n    27→    description: |\n    28→      Implement the wc word, line, and byte counter. wc depends on pkg/testutils from\n    29→      rel00.0 for differential testing and does not require pkg/sys or pkg/format.\n    30→    use_cases:\n    31→      - id: rel01.0-uc001-wc\n    32→        status: spec_complete\n    33→\n    34→  - version: \"01.1\"\n    35→    name: \"Batch 1.1 — cat specification and differential test\"\n    36→    status: spec_complete\n    37→    description: |\n    38→      Implement cat for file concatenation and display. cat depends on pkg/testutils from\n    39→      rel00.0 for differential testing and does not require pkg/sys or pkg/format.\n    40→    use_cases:\n    41→      - id: rel01.1-uc001-cat\n    42→        status: spec_complete\n    43→\n    44→  - version: \"01.2\"\n    45→    name: \"Batch 1.2 — sponge specification and differential test\"\n    46→    status: spec_complete\n    47→    description: |\n    48→      Implement sponge for soak-before-write stdin buffering. sponge depends on\n    49→      pkg/testutils from rel00.0 for differential testing and does not require pkg/sys\n    50→      or pkg/format.\n    51→    use_cases:\n    52→      - id: rel01.2-uc001-sponge\n    53→        status: spec_complete\n    54→\n    55→  - version: \"01.3\"\n    56→    name: \"Batch 1.3 — du specification and differential test\"\n    57→    status: spec_complete\n    58→    description: |\n    59→      Implement du for recursive directory disk usage reporting. du depends on\n    60→      pkg/testutils from rel00.0 for differential testing and requires pkg/sys and\n    61→      pkg/format for extended file metadata and human-readable size formatting.\n    62→    use_cases:\n    63→      - id: rel01.3-uc001-du\n    64→        status: spec_complete\n    65→\n    66→  - version: \"02.0\"\n    67→    name: \"Batch 2 — trivial utilities (true, false, yes, basename, dirname)\"\n    68→    status: pending\n    69→    description: |\n    70→      Implement five trivial utilities that require minimal logic and no shared library\n    71→      dependencies beyond pkg/testutils. true and false are exit-code-only programs. yes\n    72→      outputs repeated lines. basename and dirname perform string-based path manipulation.\n    73→      All are verified by differential testing against GNU coreutils reference binaries.\n    74→    use_cases:\n    75→      - id: rel02.0-uc001-true\n    76→        status: pending\n    77→      - id: rel02.0-uc002-false\n    78→        status: pending\n    79→      - id: rel02.0-uc003-yes\n    80→        status: pending\n    81→      - id: rel02.0-uc004-basename\n    82→        status: pending\n    83→      - id: rel02.0-uc005-dirname\n    84→        status: pending\n    85→\n    86→  - version: \"02.1\"\n    87→    name: \"Batch 2.1 — tee specification and differential test\"\n    88→    status: pending\n    89→    description: |\n    90→      Implement tee for copying stdin to stdout and one or more output files simultaneously.\n    91→      tee depends on pkg/testutils from rel00.0 for differential testing. Supports append\n    92→      mode (-a) and SIGINT suppression (-i).\n    93→    use_cases:\n    94→      - id: rel02.1-uc001-tee\n    95→        status: pending\n    96→\n    97→  - version: \"02.2\"\n    98→    name: \"Batch 2.2 — head specification and differential test\"\n    99→    status: pending\n   100→    description: |\n   101→      Implement head for printing the first N lines or bytes of files. head depends on\n   102→      pkg/testutils from rel00.0 for differential testing. Supports line-count (-n),\n   103→      byte-count (-c), negative counts, and multi-file headers with -q/-v control.\n   104→    use_cases:\n   105→      - id: rel02.2-uc001-head\n   106→        status: pending\n   107→\n   108→  - version: \"99.0\"\n   109→    name: \"Deferred — ls core specification and differential test\"\n   110→    status: spec_complete\n   111→    description: |\n   112→      ls core covers the most common flags (default, -1, -l, -a, -A, -d, --color, -h).\n   113→      Deferred from rel02.0 because ls has blocked every generation run due to task\n   114→      complexity and rate-limit constraints. The dependency chain shows ls is not required\n   115→      by other utilities in rel00.0 through rel02.0.\n   116→    use_cases:\n   117→      - id: rel99.0-uc001-ls\n   118→        status: spec_complete\n   119→\n   120→  - version: \"99.1\"\n   121→    name: \"Deferred — ls extended specification and differential test\"\n   122→    status: spec_complete\n   123→    description: |\n   124→      Extend ls with