{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012WPoWsdEvQYjrVQHABT6ur","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (72KB). Full output saved to: /home/crumbs/.claude/projects/-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-203/8b8e2752-e0d3-4adb-aeb5-99f03f790516/tool-results/b11b1dmq1.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\nid: utilities\ntitle: \"Unix Utility Catalog\"\n\noverview: |\n  Complete catalog of all utilities across the four source repositories. Each entry\n  records: description, implementation language and source file(s), approximate LOC,\n  internal shared code, required Go packages, and a profile block for implementation\n  planning.\n\n  Go package shorthand:\n    testutils   — pkg/testutils (differential testing harness; applies to ALL utilities)\n    sys/stat    — pkg/sys Stat/Lstat (extended metadata: st_nlink, st_ino, st_dev, st_blocks)\n    sys/tty     — pkg/sys TerminalWidth + IsTerminal (TIOCGWINSZ ioctl)\n    sys/sigpipe — pkg/sys InstallSIGPIPEHandler (suppress broken-pipe errors)\n    sys/sigwinch — pkg/sys OnTerminalResize (reflow on terminal resize)\n    fmt/human   — pkg/format HumanSize (human-readable byte sizes for -h)\n    fmt/columns — pkg/format Columns + PadRight/PadLeft (multi-column layout)\n    fmt/color   — pkg/format FileTypeColor (ANSI color by file type)\n\n  Coreutils internal shared code:\n    copy_engine   — copy.c, copy-file-data.c, force-link.c (cp, mv, install)\n    remove_engine — remove.c (rm, cp, mv)\n    expand_common — expand-common.c (expand, unexpand)\n    chown_engine  — chown-core.c (chown, chgrp)\n    ls_engine     — ls.c with compile-time defaults (ls, dir, vdir)\n    uname_engine  — uname.c (uname, arch)\n    group_list    — group-list.c (id, groups)\n    show_date     — show-date.c (date, touch)\n    operand2sig   — operand2sig.c (kill)\n  Moreutils internal shared code:\n    physmem       — physmem.c (sponge, parallel)\n\n  Profile taxonomy\n  ────────────────\n  type:\n    os_wrapper      — thin wrapper around one or two syscalls; trivial dispatch logic\n    stream_transform — reads bytes/lines, applies stateless transformation, writes output\n    stream_stateful  — stream with bounded state between records (counter, previous line, etc.)\n    stream_accumulate — must buffer all input before producing output\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EbL9EiwfcGCQq9hrFV7MRQ","session_id":"8b8e2752-e0d3-4adb-aeb5-99f03f790516","uuid":"d7a5aaad-8f83-4489-a65d-802a8a71ac1d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EbL9EiwfcGCQq9hrFV7MRQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are the complete contents of the three files you requested:\n\n## 1. prd020-true.yaml\n\n```yaml\nid: prd020-true\ntitle: \"cmd/true: Exit Successfully\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts use true as a no-op command that always succeeds. It appears in conditional\n  expressions, while loops (while true; do ...; done), and as a placeholder in pipelines.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtrue, installed by\n  coreutils) in exit code behavior and output, verified by differential testing via\n  pkg/testutils under LC_ALL=C.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Exit with status 0 unconditionally, matching GNU true exit behavior.\n  - G2: Handle --help and --version flags, matching GNU true flag handling.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Exit status\n    items:\n      - R1.1: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with no arguments.\n      - R1.2: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with any arguments that are not --help or --version. Arguments are not parsed, validated, or acted upon; they are silently ignored.\n      - R1.3: Must not read from stdin under any circumstances.\n      - R1.4: Must not write to stdout or stderr under normal operation (no arguments or unrecognized arguments).\n\n  R2:\n    title: Flag handling (--help, --version)\n    items:\n      - R2.1: When --help is the first argument, must print a usage message to stdout and exit 0. Remaining arguments after --help are ignored.\n      - R2.2: When --version is the first argument, must print version information to stdout and exit 0. Remaining arguments after --version are ignored.\n      - R2.3: Only the first argument is checked for --help and --version. If --help or --version appears in any position other than the first argument, it is ignored and true exits 0 silently.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Operand behavior\n    items:\n      - R3.1: All operands (non-flag arguments) are silently ignored. true does not distinguish between flags and operands; everything except --help and --version as the first argument is discarded.\n      - R3.2: The \"--\" end-of-options marker has no special meaning to true. It is ignored like any other argument.\n\n  R4:\n    title: SIGPIPE handling\n    items:\n      - R4.1: |\n          Must install a SIGPIPE handler at startup using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler, matching\n          the pattern used by other utilities in the project (see cmd/cat/main.go). This ensures\n          silent exit when stdout is closed by a downstream consumer in a pipeline.\n\n  R5:\n    title: Error handling and exit codes\n    items:\n      - R5.1: Must exit 0 in all cases except a write error during --help or --version output.\n      - R5.2: If a write error occurs while printing --help or --version output (e.g., SIGPIPE or full disk), must exit 1.\n      - R5.3: \"Error messages for write failures must be written to stderr in the format: \\\"true: <error description>\\\".\"\n      - R5.4: Must not exit with any status other than 0 or 1.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/true does not implement any flags beyond --help and --version.\n  - cmd/true does not perform any computation or I/O beyond the optional help/version output.\n  - cmd/true does not read from stdin or process piped input.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: go run ./cmd/true; echo $? prints 0.\"\n  - \"AC2: go run ./cmd/true foo bar --baz; echo $? prints 0.\"\n  - \"AC3: go run ./cmd/true --help prints a usage message to stdout and exits 0.\"\n  - \"AC4: go run ./cmd/true --version prints version information to stdout and exits 0.\"\n  - \"AC5: Differential test against gtrue passes with LC_ALL=C for no-args, arbitrary-args, and single-unrecognized-flag cases, comparing exit codes.\"\n  - \"AC6: Differential test verifies no stdout or stderr output when invoked without --help or --version, under LC_ALL=C.\"\n  - \"AC7: cmd/true compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n```\n\n## 2. road-map.yaml\n\n```yaml\nid: go-unix-utils-roadmap\ntitle: \"go-unix-utils Release Road Map\"\n\nreleases:\n  - version: \"00.0\"\n    name: \"Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure\"\n    status: spec_complete\n    description: |\n      Specify and verify the build lifecycle and shared library infrastructure that all\n      subsequent releases depend on. This release covers magefiles/ (build, lint, clean,\n      install targets and cmd/version), pkg/testutils (differential testing harness),\n      pkg/sys (syscall abstractions), and pkg/format (output formatting). The cmd/version\n      binary is the first compiled artifact and the smoke test for the build pipeline.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n        status: spec_complete\n      - id: rel00.0-uc002-format\n        status: spec_complete\n      - id: rel00.0-uc003-sys\n        status: spec_complete\n      - id: rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n        status: spec_complete\n\n  - version: \"01.0\"\n    name: \"Batch 1 — wc specification and differential test\"\n    status: spec_complete\n    description: |\n      Implement the wc word, line, and byte counter. wc depends on pkg/testutils from\n      rel00.0 for differential testing and does not require pkg/sys or pkg/format.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel01.0-uc001-wc\n        status: spec_complete\n\n  - version: \"01.1\"\n    name: \"Batch 1.1 — cat specification and differential test\"\n    status: spec_complete\n    description: |\n      Implement cat for file concatenation and display. cat depends on pkg/testutils from\n      rel00.0 for differential testing and does not require pkg/sys or pkg/format.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel01.1-uc001-cat\n        status: spec_complete\n\n  - version: \"01.2\"\n    name: \"Batch 1.2 — sponge specification and differential test\"\n    status: spec_complete\n    description: |\n      Implement sponge for soak-before-write stdin buffering. sponge depends on\n      pkg/testutils from rel00.0 for differential testing and does not require pkg/sys\n      or pkg/format.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel01.2-uc001-sponge\n        status: spec_complete\n\n  - version: \"01.3\"\n    name: \"Batch 1.3 — du specification and differential test\"\n    status: spec_complete\n    description: |\n      Implement du for recursive directory disk usage reporting. du depends on\n      pkg/testutils from rel00.0 for differential testing and requires pkg/sys and\n      pkg/format for extended file metadata and human-readable size formatting.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel01.3-uc001-du\n        status: spec_complete\n\n  - version: \"02.0\"\n    name: \"Batch 2 — trivial utilities (true, false, yes, basename, dirname)\"\n    status: pending\n    description: |\n      Implement five trivial utilities that require minimal logic and no shared library\n      dependencies beyond pkg/testutils. true and false are exit-code-only programs. yes\n      outputs repeated lines. basename and dirname perform string-based path manipulation.\n      All are verified by differential testing against GNU coreutils reference binaries.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel02.0-uc001-true\n        status: pending\n      - id: rel02.0-uc002-false\n        status: pending\n      - id: rel02.0-uc003-yes\n        status: pending\n      - id: rel02.0-uc004-basename\n        status: pending\n      - id: rel02.0-uc005-dirname\n        status: pending\n\n  - version: \"02.1\"\n    name: \"Batch 2.1 — tee specification and differential test\"\n    status: pending\n    description: |\n      Implement tee for copying stdin to stdout and one or more output files simultaneously.\n      tee depends on pkg/testutils from rel00.0 for differential testing. Supports append\n      mode (-a) and SIGINT suppression (-i).\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel02.1-uc001-tee\n        status: pending\n\n  - version: \"02.2\"\n    name: \"Batch 2.2 — head specification and differential test\"\n    status: pending\n    description: |\n      Implement head for printing the first N lines or bytes of files. head depends on\n      pkg/testutils from rel00.0 for differential testing. Supports line-count (-n),\n      byte-count (-c), negative counts, and multi-file headers with -q/-v control.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel02.2-uc001-head\n        status: pending\n\n  - version: \"99.0\"\n    name: \"Deferred — ls core specification and differential test\"\n    status: spec_complete\n    description: |\n      ls core covers the most common flags (default, -1, -l, -a, -A, -d, --color, -h).\n      Deferred from rel02.0 because ls has blocked every generation run due to task\n      complexity and rate-limit constraints. The dependency chain shows ls is not required\n      by other utilities in rel00.0 through rel02.0.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel99.0-uc001-ls\n        status: spec_complete\n\n  - version: \"99.1\"\n    name: \"Deferred — ls extended specification and differential test\"\n    status: spec_complete\n    description: |\n      Extend ls with flags requiring heavier normalization or more complex layout logic:\n      -C (forced multi-column), -x (horizontal), sort flags (-t, -S, -r, -U, -v),\n      metadata display (-i inode, -s blocks, -n numeric IDs), -F classify, -R recursive.\n      Depends on rel99.0.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel99.1-uc001-ls-extended\n        status: spec_complete\n\n  - version: \"99.2\"\n    name: \"Deferred — ts specification and differential test\"\n    status: spec_complete\n    description: |\n      Implement ts for prepending timestamps to stdin lines. Deferred from rel01.0 because\n      ts has failed in multiple generation runs due to task complexity from subrequirements\n      (R1-R8) and rate-limit constraints. Moved to deferred status pending cobbler-scaffold\n      improvements to subrequirement handling.\n    use_cases:\n      - id: rel99.2-uc001-ts\n        status: spec_complete\n```\n\n## 3. uti